From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:10:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: power chip off while no interface is up

With all radios disabled, firmware runs, the host keeps driver own
and WFDMA stays enabled, so a board draws more power than after
module removal. The driver powers the chip off 30 seconds after the
last interface goes down, or 120 seconds after probe if no interface
comes up. The delays cover a wifi reload with a radio setup retry and
the radio start of netifd after modules load. Power-off pauses the
WED PCIe poll and stops WED, because a poll of a chip under firmware
own times out. Power-on runs in the mac80211 start callback with the
hardware restart of full reset, while mac80211, rings, NAPI and WED
attachment stay in place.

While the chip is off, MCU commands, chip reads of other tasks and a
debugfs full recovery request fail with -ENODEV. Only WFDMA, TOP and
PCIe MAC registers stay accessible, because the safety of WFSYS
access is unknown. The driver tries a refused or failed power-off
again after 30 seconds, up to six attempts, because a stale reset bit
refuses every attempt. A failed power-off queues a full reset,
because firmware state is unknown, and a failed power-on leaves the
chip off. The reset work drops a recovery request under the device
mutex, because power-on reloads firmware and judges its restart by
the reset bit. LED, cooling and temperature limit settings made while
the chip is off apply at power-on or radio start, but the driver
drops an RTS threshold.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
